xt{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ 4+\\text{nullity}(A) & =7 \\\\ \\text{nullity}(A) & =7-4 \\\\ \\text{dim(Null}(A)) & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186522756 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184171 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d562ea0c-94f3-5fe6-ba82-c651a51d0bbe" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Rank or Nullity of a Matrix Given a Description of the Column or Null Space"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5e0e3711-6463-5725-af73-097d1ae29a9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522214} {:answer/id #uuid "61446332-0629-5ef8-8fdd-ddaab16f7297" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522220} {:answer/id #uuid "8522d96b-7f5f-51ec-a409-3570be436a9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522286} {:answer/id #uuid "8b68a9a3-d2ff-5fe6-a44b-0661eda03baf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522303} {:answer/id #uuid "d3e1f722-dade-587d-89a7-857b88b1ecf7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522459}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8b68a9a3-d2ff-5fe6-a44b-0661eda03baf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522303} :answer-field/id #uuid "30e4bc43-9fa2-56e5-9887-5f6820f6d33f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522580}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "900f650b-6d73-5995-901b-d7a17074a6aa" :question/math-academy-id "q-141232" :question/problem "Let $A$ be a $6\\times 10$ matrix. If $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3},{b}_{4}\\}$ is a basis of $\\text{Col}(A)$, find $\\text{dim(Null}(A)).$" :question/worked-solution "According to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nFor the given matrix, we have $n=10,$ and since $B$ is formed by $4$ vectors, $\\text{rank}(A)=4.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ 4+\\text{nullity}(A) & =10 \\\\ \\text{nullity}(A) & =10-4 \\\\ \\text{dim(Null}(A)) & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186522771 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184219 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fcbc10c0-4e6b-5dac-ad87-f0175e4a53d2" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Rank or Nullity of a Matrix Using the Rank-Nullity Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0489d7c0-9892-5b4f-a265-35a855cae665" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522025} {:answer/id #uuid "19d7b093-ccfa-5074-9a83-a27b17ba1454" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522078} {:answer/id #uuid "40c69629-2803-5ad7-aa97-c2b10a5bb2b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522158} {:answer/id #uuid "9b640a26-d27a-5063-8ab1-f9eddbf076e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522337} {:answer/id #uuid "f26141c5-5ae9-5b4b-80af-055e70b6a825" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522536}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "19d7b093-ccfa-5074-9a83-a27b17ba1454" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522078} :answer-